name><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>MacLennan</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Sedmak</surname><given-names>DD</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Analysis of the molecular quality of human tissues: an experience from the Cooperative Human Tissue Network</article-title><source>Am J Clin Pathol</source><year>2002</year><volume>118</volume><fpage>733</fpage><lpage>741</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Am J Clin Pathol||118|733||bib7|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12428794</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Merz</surname><given-names>JF</given-names></name><name><surname>Saukar</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Taube</surname><given-names>SE</given-names></name><name><surname>LiVolsi</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Use of human tissues in research: clarifying clinician and research roles and information flows</article-title><source>J Invest Med</source><year>1997</year><volume>45</volume><fpage>252</fpage><lpage>257</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'J Invest Med||45|252||bib8|'--></citation></ref><ref id="bib9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Naber</surname><given-names>SP</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Continuing role of a frozen-tissue bank in molecular pathology</article-title><source>Diagn Mol Pathol</source><year>1996</year><volume>5</volume><fpage>253</fpage><lpage>259</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Diagn Mol Pathol||5|253||bib9|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8955616</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Naber</surname><given-names>SP</given-names></name><name><surname>Smith</surname><given-names>LL</given-names></name><name><surname>Wolfe</surname><given-names>HJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Role of the frozen tissue bank in molecular pathology</article-title><source>Diagn Mol Pathol</source><year>1992</year><volume>1</volume><fpage>73</fpage><lpage>79</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Diagn Mol Pathol||1|73||bib10|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1342956</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib11"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Qualman</surname><given-names>SJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Bowen</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Brewer-Swartz</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>France</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The role of tumor banking and related informatics in molecular research</article-title><source>Expression Profiling of Human Tumors: Diagnostic and Research Applications</source><year>2003</year><publisher-name>Humana Press Inc: Totowa, NJ</publisher-name><fpage>103</fpage><lpage>117</lpage>Ladanyi M, Gerald W (eds) pp</citation></ref><ref id="bib12"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Report of the Intergroup Specimen Banking Committee</collab></person-group><article-title/><year>1999</year>Cancer Therapy Evaluation Program, Division of Cancer Treatment and Diagnosis, National Cancer Institute, May 31, 1999 (on file</citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>